# A shell script must reach the server with LF endings. `install.sh` is piped
# to `bash` by the documented one-liner, so a stray CR turns a command into
# "command\r" and bash reports `command not found` - which is exactly the
# unexplained `/tmp/inst.sh: line 698: +: command not found` seen on a real
# Ubuntu host during testing.
#
# This repository had core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, so a CRLF
# checkout was silently produced here and then committed. Pin the text files
# that are executed or hashed to LF regardless of the developer's platform,
# and stop git from rewriting them on the way back in.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
VERSION text eol=lf